Error: Jet.AliasWithoutParameters: A type alias of a plain type needs type parameters — write `Name<T>: …`
  --> Tests/UI/type_alias_no_params.jet:1:1
    |
  1 | Meters: Float
    | ^^^^^^
 Why: A transparent type alias is only for shortening generic spellings, so one without type parameters names a generic application such as `Set<Int>`
 Fix: For a distinct type name over a primitive, use `Name: distinct BaseType` instead
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.AliasWithoutParameters
